# MON-1 — Foundation Monitoring & Observability

MON-1 **consolidates** existing observability signals into one explainable
`GO | WATCH | FAIL | UNKNOWN` decision. It must never duplicate or weaken:
NSF-9 smoke/release-safety, NSF-10 release evidence, NSF-R011/R012, CICD-CTRL-1,
POST-ENT runtime hardening, the ENT-8/LB-1 health endpoints, deploy/backup
evidence, or the domain audit commands.

Durable rules:

1. Consolidate existing signals; never re-implement a health probe, smoke gate,
   deploy-evidence pipeline, CI classifier, or domain audit.
2. The monitoring UI (`/foundation/monitoring`) is read-only, Super-Admin-only
   (`permission:view_developer_console`, no new permission), and never mutates
   runtime state (no log clear, no queue retry/delete, no chmod).
3. No secrets / environment values / DB credentials / tokens / raw stack traces /
   KTP-NIK / raw failed-job payloads / full log payloads in UI or JSON. Route free
   text through `SensitiveValueMasker`.
4. No expensive command runs on a web request. Audit execution is CLI-only via
   `--include-audits`; the web page reads cached evidence metadata. In
   `config/foundation_monitoring.php`, any `type: command` signal MUST have
   `auto_run: false`.
5. Existing audit commands (`inventory:procurement-workflow-audit`,
   `rme:doctor-performance-access-audit`) stay authoritative; MON-1 only reports
   their exit status.
6. Storage/cache writability (`storage/framework/cache/data`, `storage/logs`,
   `bootstrap/cache`) must be observable (temp-file probe, report-only, never
   chmod).
7. Every GO/WATCH/FAIL/UNKNOWN decision must carry reasons + safe remediation.
8. `--strict` exits non-zero only on real unsafe FAIL; WATCH/UNKNOWN never fail
   unless `--fail-on-warning`.

Command: `php artisan foundation:monitoring-observability-check [--json] [--strict] [--include-audits]`.
